The formula is:
∫[a,b] f(x)dx ≈ (h/2) * [f(x₀) + 2f(x₁) + 2f(x₂) + ... + 2f(xₙ₋₁) + f(xₙ)]

where h = (b - a) / N and xᵢ = a + i*h

Let me implement this:

```cpp
double h = (b - a) / N;
double result = (f(a) + f(b)) / 2.0;

for (int i = 1; i < N; i++) {
    double x = a + i * h;
    result += f(x);
}

result *= h;
return result;
```

This is the standard implementation of the trapezoidal rule.

